 "text": "Hi, how you doing right now? Mostly the language. If the book is simple, an English speaker with good vocabulary and a bit of patience will get through it. The grammar is usually the hard part. Dutch has a lot of words you don't use in English, like two verb forms and a separate tense for the phone. It is once you get used to it. Norwegian is even simpler. That can be tricky. Many Dutch sounds don't exist in English, and words like rhubarb or stroopwafel sound strange. I' say Norwegian is gentler. It has fewer long words and fewer cases, and the grammar is mostly simple. You might be surprised. Try reading a short story or a travel guide in the language of your travel plans. It' lot more fun than a language book.",
